      <h2>What every review contains</h2>
      <p>Each BuildNReview article follows the same structure so you can compare products quickly: a short verdict, pros and cons, a score breakdown, real use cases, full specifications and a clear "who should buy it" answer.</p>

      <h2>The four scores</h2>
      <p>Every product is scored out of 10 on four criteria. The wording changes per category (a printer's "performance" is print speed, a vacuum's is suction and pick-up) but the weights never do:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Performance (35%)</strong>: how well it does its main job. Print speed and reliability, drilling power, cutting depth, cleaning results.</li>
        <li><strong>Build quality (25%)</strong>: materials, finish, precision and how it is likely to hold up over years.</li>
        <li><strong>Ease of use (20%)</strong>: unboxing and setup, software, daily handling, maintenance and cleaning.</li>
        <li><strong>Value (20%)</strong>: what you get for the money compared with direct rivals.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The overall score is the weighted average, rounded to one decimal place. As a guide: 9.0 and above is outstanding, 8.0–8.9 is very good to excellent, 7.0–7.9 is good with clear trade-offs, and anything below 7 has problems we would warn a friend about.</p>

      <h2>Preview reviews</h2>
      <p>Some reviews are marked <strong>Preview review</strong>. These are compiled from manufacturer specifications, official documentation and published information before our own hands-on test is complete. Their scores are provisional and are updated once testing is finished.</p>

      <h2>Prices</h2>
      <p>Prices are US list prices at the time of the last update. Retailers change prices often, so always check the current price through the link on the review.</p>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>Brands do not see reviews before publication and cannot pay for a better score. Some links earn us a commission; see our <a href="/en/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> for details.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
